    "final_answer": "I have gathered all the information needed. Let me provide the final answer.\n\n---\n\n# Coursera Course: Sustainable Agricultural Land Management (可持续农田管理)\n\n**URL:** https://www.coursera.org/learn/sustainable-agriculture\n\n## Course Overview\n\n- **Provider:** University of Florida\n- **Level:** Beginner\n- **Modules:** 8\n- **Enrollment:** 59,069 students\n- **Rating:** 4.8/5 stars (675 reviews)\n\n## Course Objectives\n\nThe course introduces agricultural and urban water quality challenges, particularly in Florida, exploring their foundations, along with land and nutrient management strategies, and the science and policy behind Best Management Practices (BMPs). By the end of the course, students will be able to:\n\n- Describe Florida's water quality issues and the regulatory framework driving water quality management.\n- Evaluate the science and policy supporting Best Management Practices (BMPs) for agriculture.\n- Assess BMP research and analyze its role in determining practices and policies for protecting water quality.\n\n### Modules Covered:\n\n1. **Introduction to Sustainable Agricultural Land Management** (可持续农业土地管理入门)\n2. **Water Quality Issues and Regulations** (水质问题和法规)\n3. **TMDLs and Nutrients** (TMDL 与营养物质)\n4. **Best Management Practices** (最佳管理实践)\n5. **Soil Management** (土壤管理)\n6. **Nutrient Management** (养分管理)\n7. **Agricultural Water Use** (农业用水)\n8. **Agricultural Irrigation Management** (农业灌溉管理)\n\n## Lead Instructor Background\n\n**George J. Hochmuth, Ph.D.** — Professor, University of Florida\n\n- **Affiliation:** University of Florida (Department of Soils, Institute of Food and Agricultural Sciences — IFAS)\n- **Faculty Profile:** http://soils.ifas.ufl.edu/personnel/Hochmuth/index.htm\n- **Instructor Rating:** 4.8/5 (244 reviews)\n- **Courses on Coursera:** 1 course (Sustainable Agricultural Land Management) with 59,069 students\n\n### Research Focus\n\nHis research program addresses environmental science questions pertaining to water quality and nutrient/water management in urban and agricultural settings. His work specifically focuses on:\n\n- Addressing **nitrogen and phosphorus** nutrient management questions\n- Investigating sources of nutrients found in groundwater and surface water\n- Studying how **irrigation and fertilization management practices** work together to prevent nitrogen losses from fields and landscapes\n- Developing **best management practices** for keeping nutrients and water in the plant root zone\n- Creating new tools (plant and soil testing meters, application devices, computer programs) to help individuals improve their nutrient and water management capabilities\n- Identifying crop and landscape plant **cultivars** that are more efficient in nutrient uptake and utilization\n- Exploring roles of crop selection, rotation, cover-cropping, mulching, irrigation, and fertilization in a systems approach to minimize nutrient losses\n- Examining the role of organic nutrient sources in fertilization\n\n### Methodology\n\nDr. Hochmuth conducts research across various settings — greenhouses for small bench-scale studies, field-scale studies in residential landscapes and on farms, and specialized techniques like hydroponics to study nutrient uptake and utilization.\n\nHis expertise makes him exceptionally qualified to teach this course, given his direct research focus on the intersection of agricultural practices, water quality, and sustainable nutrient/water management — the exact core of this course.",
